WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.510
Excuse me. Are you using this chair?

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:03.910
Yes.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.550
Pete, hi! Thanks for meeting me.

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.230
Sure. But I don’t have lots of time, Anna.

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.870
I’m busy looking for work.

6
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.330
Pete, you can tear these want ads up and throw them away!

7
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.830
I have good news!

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.030
Anna, I was working on that crossword puzzle.

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.090
Oh. Sorry. Sorry.

10
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.750
Pete, forget about the crossword puzzle.

11
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.390
I have a job offer for you!

12
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.390
I'm listening.

13
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.410
My boss wants me to team up with someone to host a talk show.

14
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.950
But the person must be different from me.

15
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.810
So, I thought of you.

16
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.750
Different from you? What do you mean?

17
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.950
I'm sorry, Pete, I don't have time right now.

18
00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.910
Here's my boss's address.

19
00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.970
Your interview is tomorrow morning at 10 am.

20
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.210
But what do you mean “different”?

21
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.790
Just be yourself, Pete.

22
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.350
Just be yourself.

23
00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.290
Did you find any two-word verbs?

24
00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.090
Here’s one example.

25
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.550
Pete can throw the want ads away!

26
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.990
Throw away is a two-word verb.

27
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.950
Thanks for coming in, Pete.

28
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.430
Thanks for the opportunity, Ms. Weaver.

29
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:34.090
I need to find out if you have the skills for this job.

30
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.730
And I want you to be completely honest.

31
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.170
Okay.

32
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.470
First, let's talk about your personal skills.

33
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.650
Pete, are you a people person?

34
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:59.590
Well, okay, sometimes I think people talk too much.

35
00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:06.150
Pete, what work of yours are you most proud of?

36
00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.970
Last year, I locked myself in a cabin and wrote a book.

37
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.510
I didn't speak to anybody the entire time!

38
00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.890
It was the best two months of my life.

39
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.610
Okay. I think I’ve heard enough.
